  "f1_design": {
    "precedent_reuse": "Meaning is rederived into SEC009. OS015 establishes a reusable L4 pattern: preserve ordered findings and distinguish overall classification from axis state; its model also specifies an OS015-specific severity order, which is not imported into SEC009. SEC009 uses no new cross-axis severity order.",
    "sec009_formation_rule": "Findings use existing L4 scalar sort (code,pointer,return_owner), preserving duplicate codes at distinct pointers. expected.finding_codes is the ordered code sequence. expected_axis is an ordered list of existing axes contributed by each ordered finding; a shared source finding can contribute multiple independently evaluated axes in contract dependency order. expected_classification is the existing overall result.condition. The scalar expected_state required by the existing class key is copied from the existing single-axis classification for the first ordered axis; all axis states remain separately listed in order. No cross-axis severity priority or aggregation rule is introduced. No finding, axis, owner, result, authority, or operation effect is synthesized.",
